"PHASE 2 LANDED: INVENTORY + LOADOUT CUSTOMIZATION (2026-08-12). Loadout model per user: ONE clothing/armor slot + up to FOUR relics applied across all stances; each stance gets assigned armaments. Server: armors + relics asset kinds (public, name-canonical push); ItemRef enum (Armament/Armor/Relic by id; authored as ItemRefAsset by name); ItemComponent makes an entity BE an item; CARRYING IS LOCATION (user): items in inventory have the carrier as location; entity_deletion_timer_system now spills a destroyed carrier's contents out to the carrier's own location (stranded contents logged when the carrier had none). Take/Drop ActionEffects implemented in event resolution (take pulls a co-located item in; drop pushes a carried item to the room); ActionType::Inventory targeting = item within reach (co-located or carried). ArmorComponent (single slot) + RelicsComponent, both dirties(equipment flag); StanceLoadoutsComponent (per-stance armament asset-id assignments, never blob-authored); equipment cache = flat EquipmentComponent (NPC/blob path) + armor + relics, pass now always runs and clears its flag. Reducers: set_armor/clear_armor/set_relics (cap 4)/assign_stance_armaments -- ownership validated by COUNTING carried items per asset (counted-multiset: dual-wield needs two owned blades), and assign validates GRIP feasibility on the candidate context (base + gear + stance hand >= 0) at preparation time per the design; set_stance re-arms from the assignment when the player has loadouts (NPCs keep flat equipment). Content: take/drop actions (take needs hand>=1) granted by human/bandit bodies; 3 armors, 5 relics; the keep's armament decorations are now REAL takeable items, sanctum scatters staff/relics/robe items. Client: gear tables public for backward name lookup; LoadoutPanel (armor slot, relic toggles w/ 4-cap display, per-stance armament instance toggles over counted ids) living in the dynamic panel's equipment mode; inventory mode already lists carried items via containment; Inventory actions in actionOptions (targetHasItem). Tests: 105 unit (LoadoutPanel x3, actionOptions inventory case), e2e phase 9-loadout (take moves item into player; unowned armor rejected + owned armor's defense flows to hp; assignment + swap arms the blade stance -- incl. the subtle case that dueling stays unreachable until the sword is in the CURRENT stance's hands; 4-relic cap), full ladder 0-9 green, cargo test + clippy 0 errors, production pack re-validated. Registered test-e2e-loadout. DESIGN NOTES from user recorded this session, deferred: (1) small entities may sneak INTO larger entities -- containment as an implicit path, size-gated; (2) size comparisons should restrict usable weapons/armor, and size-change effects should propagate to carried entities (your gear shrinks with you, normally); (3) size play space: tiny/giant kingdoms; pocket vehicles grown to ride or shrunk into (implies a piloting mechanic); shrink effects that disable gear; powerful items requiring resizing to use; (4) text-based freedom: abstract locations -- text, colors, musical notes as places to hold, visit, or travel through. All connect to the granular size stat + relations design."